From e2e5d58d2e364629248f0d22c4026495d3ec11af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:42:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0039] drm/a9_eink: latch a rail fault when the FP9929A drops
 out with the pipeline on

Run 11: at an update's start a9_hv_is_on() was false with the transport
on ("FP9929A dropped out while the pipeline was on"). The pipeline was
powered down, but the next update re-powered the FP9929A and submitted a
partial (clear=0) frame before the userspace watcher closed the gates.
The failed conjunct was not recorded.

Capture the failed sample and the transport state before any shutdown in
one line and in the eink status (rail_* fields): getter return, the raw
PG read (1, 0 or -errno; -ENODATA when the lookup failed), FP9929A on,
energized, forced and emergency state, transport on/gone/front_null/
interlock armed, power-session age and time since the last waveform run.
fp9929a_get_status() now reports the single PG read pg_good comes from
(pg_raw) and the energized state.

Latch a9x_rail_fault synchronously, set enable = 0 and owe a full Clear,
then run the existing ordered neutral/power-down (emergency HV removal if
the neutral fails, forced regulator off if DPMS off fails). Any latched
fault (stall or rail) refuses power-up, real updates, run_ring and every
drive commit; an enable-only write cannot bypass it. Only writing 1 to
a9_eink.clear_fault clears it; the first real update afterwards is a full
Clear (force_clear stays set until a real update completes).

No debounce, retry or automatic recovery. Frame-progress interlock, PMIC
max_on_ms/min_off_ms, bin admission, starvation latch and prefill K=12
are unchanged. Apply after 0001-0038.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
